{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>YHWH our Elohim spoke to us at Horeb, saying</b>. In my opinion, Horeb is the name of a place near Mount Sinai where Israel dwelled that year, for the desert was vast, and there was the mountain which Elohim desired, whose name is Sinai, and therefore the entire desert is called the desert of Sinai, as though it were the desert of Mount Sinai. And Scripture says (Exodus 19:2), \"And they came to the desert of Sinai and encamped in the desert, and Israel encamped there opposite the mountain\" — they encamped in the desert in a place called Horeb, which is opposite the mountain. And it is possible that both the mountain and the desert are called Sinai because there are many sneh-bushes there, and there, near the mountain, is a place or a settlement whose name is Horeb, and there they stood. And the verse that says (Exodus 3:1), \"And he came to the mountain of Elohim, to Horeb,\" means that he came to Horeb, where the mountain of Elohim is, and the bush was on the mountain, and Moses was in Horeb the place that is before it, near it, where the camp of Israel stood for a year, and therefore he said (Exodus 3:3), \"Let me turn aside now and see\" — that he would turn aside from Horeb to the mountain. And sometimes Scripture calls the mountain by this name, as it says (Exodus 33:6), \"And the children of Israel stripped themselves of their ornaments from Mount Horeb\" — meaning from the mountain that is in Horeb, within its boundary or before it, or that the entire land is called Horeb and the mountain is within it. And likewise, \"Remember the Torah of Moses My servant, which I commanded him at Horeb for all Israel — statutes and judgments\" (Malachi 3:22), alludes to everything that was commanded on the mountain and in the Tent of Meeting that was there at Horeb. And I saw in the Yalkut Shimoni their midrash: \"You did not know at Sinai, nor did you hear at Horeb, and from of old your ear was not opened\" (Isaiah 48:8), in the plains of Moab — hinting that Horeb is the place where the Tent of Meeting was. Only Rabbi Eli'ezer said (Exodus 3:1) that Horeb is Mount Sinai, for because of the heat (חֹרֶב) and dryness the sneh-bush would be found there, and it is called by two names, and both are equivalent in meaning."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:43:55.408391501Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}